{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Upon the loins.</b> It is known, and it is from the constellation of the stars of heaven and their Kasilim." "<b>Upon the kidneys.</b> Like \"the men came upon the women\" (Exodus 35:22); its meaning is 'with.' And they are called kidneys on account of the power of lust for intercourse, and it is from the root of נכספה and also כלתה נפשי."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The referent of 'their Kasilim' is cryptic; rendered literally without expansion.", 1 "The two quoted phrases (נכספה and כלתה נפשי) are left as Hebrew since they are cited as lexical proof for the root; their respective verses are Job 14:15 and not identified with certainty."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:08.774221098Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}